{"id": "EUVD-2026-48998", "enisaUuid": "a2d071f3-9028-3cf6-a5c0-e5e15060eb4f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Clear __hyp_running_vcpu when flushing the pKVM hyp vCPU\n\nflush_hyp_vcpu() copies the host vCPU context into the hyp's private\nvCPU on every run. ctxt_to_vcpu() expects a guest context to have a\nNULL __hyp_running_vcpu, which is only ever set on the host context, so\nthat it resolves the vCPU via container_of(). While this is generally\nthe case, flush_hyp_vcpu() copies the context verbatim and does not\nenforce this, so a value provided by the host is dereferenced at EL2\n(host -> EL2).\n\nFix by clearing __hyp_running_vcpu after the copy.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:49:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:21", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/477145860dba4c30f0b4e36f02f4c5291c1c888b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dfaef40d8a1533940fc1af788d70fce07362b4ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bea2f8becdb20d34378493c3b77a9b9cf8c6cfa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4f4d61715d1061ba83b88196a3605662be30750", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8042f6e1d7befb2fb6b10a75918642bcd0acf9a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64286", "GHSA-5rwh-cw23-rrm6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06c06021-ce86-30e5-aeb0-a9a6b2f639e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "be66e67f175096f283c9d5614c4991fc9e7ed975 <477145860dba4c30f0b4e36f02f4c5291c1c888b"}, {"id": "0e4f665c-c6c1-3410-be7e-193f63e69e75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "106bbf66-5a66-308e-8912-d99f87581610", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}, {"id": "115f75cf-aa7c-32c5-a023-e5da3c3ea4fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 